                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/244a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Butler</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-12-09T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 9,
                                1928—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>31. The Bolivia-Paraguay situation is giving the Department much concern. The
                    Department hesitates to make any suggestions for fear it may complicate the
                    situation, since the Government of Argentina has been mediating this question
                    for many months and any suggestions from the Government of the United States
                    might be misunderstood. However, it is the understanding of the Department that
                    Paraguay has suggested the constitution of Commission of Inquiry under the
                    Gondra Treaty, and the Department is very anxious to learn immediately Bolivia’s
                    attitude in regard thereto. Please expedite reply.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
